\subsection{Prior on the Treatment Effect ($\delta$)}
Alternatively, when researchers have specific prior beliefs or historical data regarding the relative difference between the arms, the framework parametrizes the design prior directly on the treatment effect, $\delta$. In this scenario, the evaluation metric $m$ is expressed as an integral over the prior distribution of the effect size, $p(\delta)$:
$$m = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \Prob{\text{Success} \mid \delta} p(\delta) \, d\delta$$
This parametrization is particularly useful for calculating metrics such as Assurance (Average Power) or Predictive Power, where the focus is on the probability of a successful trial given the hypothesized distribution of the drug's efficacy.



