\section{Sequential design}
Presentation of the sequential design, before the code was relying on exact numerical integration, this can be achieved also in a sequential design, 
but to compute the OC we should compute the probability of early success, but also the probability of early futility,but for example also for the final success itwouldnt be a simple integral since the outcome of the 
interim analysis and of the final data are highly correlated. This mean that for final success we should find the probability that y1 lands in teh continuation zone 
and the the final y crosses the final success. And the more stops we have the more complicated it become. That is why rely on simulation by simulating 
10000 paths of the trialswhere for given thetas we raw the interim data, apply the decision rules, drop the failed/succeded trails, and simualte the remainder to the end. 

This potentially also allow us to use more complex futility rules like predictive prob of success. 

